  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="fcd1-bc1e-bdd7-343a" name="Ligurian (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>LIGURIAN ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.76-79)
Characters up to 25%; at least one must be the overall leader. If the Prince is not the Army General the commander must be a Clan Chieftain. Warriors at least 50%; Skirmishers up to 25%.
Special rules: Warband (all Warband Psychology rules); Feigned Flight for Ligurian skirmishers only (they rally immediately after a flee or fire-and-flee charge reaction and may reform facing any direction; the charging enemy still counts as charging); Cycnus Standard Bearer (swan symbol); Ligurian Bard; Pennato (hand weapon, or like a halberd with +1 Strength two-handed); Wild Beast Skin (+1 save bonus against missile fire, combinable with a shield).
Optional variants (opponent's consent): an Apuani army ignores the 0-1 limit on Apuani and omits Capillati and Veterans; an Alpine Capillati army (1st century BC) ignores the 0-1 limit on Capillati and omits Apuani and Veterans.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Ligurian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Warriors: at least 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 25%
  Standard Ligurian composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
